                                                              "summary":  "Damodaran frames AI as having entered a critical maturation phase where it must demonstrate sustainable business fundamentals rather than hype-driven narratives. He estimates AI\u0027s total addressable market at between $6 trillion and $26 trillion depending on assumptions about labor displacement and pricing, but notes current revenue of at most $250 billion is vastly disproportionate to the $1.7 trillion already invested by major tech companies. He argues AI is now in the \u0027business-building\u0027 phase where unit economics and competitive moats become decisive, and warns that the most optimistic market-size scenarios are also the ones most damaging to incumbent businesses.",
